# Error Handling

The `onError` config callback fires whenever the active data source reports a fresh failure. It works for any `IDataSource` implementation — `FetchApiDataSource`, `ApiFunctionDataSource`, the svelte-query data source or your own custom one — because it observes the `queryResult` of the configured source rather than hooking into a specific transport.

Identical error instances are reported only once, so a transient blip won't spam your toast queue.

```typescript
const config: DataTableConfig<UserData> = {
	type: 'flakyUsers',
	columnProperties: {
		// ...
	},
	dataUniquePropertyKey: 'id',
	onError: (error) => {
		// surface the failure however you like — toast, sentry, console
		toasts.push({ id: nextToastId++, message: error.message });
	}
};
```

The example below drives an `ApiFunctionDataSource` with a deliberately flaky function. Use the slider to control the failure rate, or click "Fail the next request" to force one failure on demand.

